00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.559
So the question really is, why Toro?

00:03:39.559 --> 00:03:48.679
And I think most of you here, I assume, already know a lot of the benefits of why we love

00:03:48.679 --> 00:03:50.000
Toro.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:59.080
But to those that aren't aware yet, it comes from all the work that was done with Armour

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.699
down being bundled up.

00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:08.479
Now we have Toro, which is a literary programming device where we have a file that essentially

00:04:08.479 --> 00:04:15.360
is marked down that then can be turned into other formats like PDF, Word, HTML, so on

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.920
and so forth.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:23.399
But it's also been extended here to work with the RevealJS JavaScript framework that can

00:04:23.399 --> 00:04:25.660
create slides.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:31.779
The reason why we want to use both together is that we're getting all the benefits from

00:04:31.779 --> 00:04:33.100
Toro.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:42.260
One of them is that we have our Toro cells that render the results out as we need them.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:47.579
So instead, how you would normally do it if you did it in a Word document or a LaTeX document

00:04:47.579 --> 00:04:54.500
without using Toro or Armour down is you would have your script, run the Toro, and then copy

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.899
and paste the files over.

00:04:56.899 --> 00:05:03.820
But then the problem really becomes, what if my data changes now?

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:09.619
I need to remember which files have updated, what numbers have changed.

00:05:09.619 --> 00:05:19.260
You're just putting this chunk in your markdown file, and it will just input it in.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:24.420
But we just put all our Toro chunks in our Toro files.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:31.059
They're being rendered, moved along into our markdown files, and into the document itself.

00:05:31.059 --> 00:05:35.579
So we never have to worry about topping things over.

00:05:35.579 --> 00:05:37.140
Everything stays in one.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:48.299
And this can become less useful here in slides because it's less of a report and more of

00:05:48.339 --> 00:05:56.100
where we use slides is typically different than other types of reporting systems.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:00.339
But it's still useful getting all of these wins, especially with charts and stuff.

00:06:00.339 --> 00:06:06.059
It just works how we would expect.

00:06:06.059 --> 00:06:11.859
It's HTML native, so it is technically a web page.

00:06:11.859 --> 00:06:16.299
So I'm showing the slides right now, and it's just a website.

00:06:16.299 --> 00:06:22.220
And we are getting all the benefits from it being a website.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:27.899
So you can put animations, you can put videos, and you just embed a YouTube video in here,

00:06:27.899 --> 00:06:30.100
and it should just work.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:35.940
But we also enabled to do the code.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:37.380
We're still not like moved out.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:41.140
I'm not showing it right now because I just thought about it right now, but we still get

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:43.059
all of the latest features.

00:06:43.059 --> 00:06:49.500
So if you want to put an iteration in there, there are HTML frameworks around that that

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:51.540
Trotter just supports natively.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:58.540
So if you use late set formulas to make an iteration, it will also just render as you

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:01.859
would expect, even though it's a website.

00:07:01.859 --> 00:07:05.040
So we're really getting the best of both worlds.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:13.880
And if you really need to, there are ways to turn our slides that we're creating with

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:18.519
Trotter and reveal.js into PDFs and PowerPoint.

00:07:18.519 --> 00:07:26.160
One of them, actually, if you go to the bottom left in the slides or press M, go to tools,

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:33.320
there's this PDF export mode, clicking that and then doing like the command P or the Windows

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:37.000
equivalent to print the page.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:44.000
It will generate the PDF for us for everything that it makes sense for.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:50.279
So obviously, we can't print a bit embedded YouTube video to PDF.

00:07:50.279 --> 00:07:58.040
And likewise, if we have animations happening, slide transitions, they obviously also felt

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:01.239
like disappear.

00:08:01.239 --> 00:08:04.200
But everything else should work.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:10.440
And if it doesn't, let us know and we can fix most of these things.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:15.000
So you might want a PDF or PowerPoint.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:21.079
We can get to that most of the time, if that is the required deliverable for you.

